_build/

# Compiler output that lands beside the sources when the build is run
# in the source tree rather than under _build. These are artefacts of
# a build, never content.
*.cmi
*.cmx
*.cmo
*.o
*.a
*.annot

# The flake's output symlink. `nix build` creates it in the directory
# of the flake; it points into the store and it changes with every
# build. It is an artefact of a build, never content - and it was
# committed here by accident, which is exactly what this file is for.
result

# A compiled binary that landed in the repository by accident. The
# method is OCaml and has no business here.
a.out

# The trail: the record of what was run, where and against which
# subject. It is evidence, not content: it is regenerated by running
# the checks, and it is not carried in the repository. The method adds
# no file to a project by inertia.
.math/

# The built site. It is regenerated by `sh site/build.sh` from
# site/src, spec.json and `mathc map --json`; only the sources are
# carried in the repository.
site/dist/

# Local JavaScript dependencies and logs from the Paseo plugin toolchain.
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
